Speaker 1: And finally today, that footage that&nbsp;
Tucker Carlson got his hands on, 44000 hours of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:13.980
footage from January 6th. Security cameras all&nbsp;
over Congress given to him by Kevin McCarthy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:21.420
A coalition of news organizations are now suing&nbsp;
the federal government to get their hands on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:28.200
that very same footage that has been handed over&nbsp;
to Tucker Carlson. Those organizations include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.960
advanced publications, the Associated Press,&nbsp;
CNN, CBS, the E.W. Scripps Company, Gannett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.540
the New York Times, Politico, and ProPublica. And&nbsp;
basically what they've done is they've sued the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:45.600
federal government. Well, not necessarily sued&nbsp;
the federal government. That may be the wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.540
